// expect: 3
// Refined-alias annotations keep SCALAR comparisons — the compare dispatch
// chases TAlias/TRefined to the base type (fold_strip), never minting a
// nominal sum-compare for a refined Int. The regression this gates: with
// `pos: ValidOffset` bound as a raw TName, m3's lex_from compared positions
// via $compare_nValidOffset — scalar below heap_base (4096), TAG-COMPARE of
// dereferenced garbage above it — so every input larger than 4096 bytes
// lexed as if it ended at 4096 (the 2026-07-09 m4 collapse). Operands 4200
// and 5000 sit above heap_base by construction: the broken path returns 7,
// the honest scalar compare returns 3.
// The alias is declared LAST — the wheel's own order (types.mn sorts after
// lexer.mn in the concatenated wheel), so this also gates the pre-pass
// registration: the alias must exist in the env BEFORE the main walk
// converts vcmp's annotations, regardless of file order.
fn vcmp(a: VO, b: VO) = if a >= b { 7 } else { 3 }

fn main() = vcmp(4200, 5000)

type VO = Int where 0 <= self
